      "message": "fix(motion): the plan's crossing check reads a shared end a rounding apart as a touch\n\nThe adaptive planner's self-crossing check (adaptive/guard.rs) tested\nexact signs, so two walks that meet at one vertex reached twice - an\norbit closing a ulp off its start, a microlift return landing on a chord\nend, a ring starting on the last ring's vertex - could read as a proper\ncrossing and send a good level to Offset rings.\n\nThe scan now asks `crosses`: the proper-crossing test with \"on the\nother chord's line\" read to within TOUCH = 1e-9 mm instead of an exact\nzero. Every contact the old law accepted exactly (shared vertex, T-touch,\ncollinear retrace) is now accepted a rounding off too; a real crossing\nstill crosses. A non-finite point reads as a crossing instead of being\ndropped by the length filter. `proper` (used by lift_link) is unchanged.\n\nFixes #1048\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
